    <h2>Initiative 3: Bridge the Hand-off Gap &amp; System Governance</h2>

    <h3>The Challenge</h3>
    <p>A classic failure mode for enterprise design systems is that beautiful Figma libraries fail to match the real code shipped in production. Without strict governance and active communication, developers make assumptions and design fidelity drifts.</p>

    <h3>The Governance Strategy</h3>
    <p>I acted as the primary bridge between our design squads and engineering pods. We set up an operating rhythm designed to prevent surprises at the sprint finish line:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Weekly System Reviews:</strong> Ran recurring open office hours where product designers could bring proposed new patterns to evaluate whether they belonged in the core library or should remain local.</li>
      <li><strong>Figma Dev Mode Annotations:</strong> Standardized documentation standards directly inside Figma, explicitly detailing responsive behavior, edge cases, error states, and token names.</li>
      <li><strong>Code Auditing:</strong> Regularly paired with front-end developers to review live staging builds, verifying that tokens were implemented correctly in CSS and React.</li>
    </ul>

